  "query_preview": "..\nIssued at 1242 AM CDT Sun Sep 20 2026\n\nOne more day of high temperatures 15 to 20 degrees above normal\ncan be expected today with highs in the middle to upper 90s. A \ncold front will push through the PAH forecast area late today \nand tonight, finally ending the prolonged heat wave. Temperatures\ntonight and Monday will still be 5 to 15 degrees above normal, \nbut much cooler air will really filter in by Monday night into \nTuesday. Readings Tuesday through the end of the week and even \ninto next weekend will be near to a little below normal, with\nhighs generally in the middle 70s to around 80 degrees, and \nlows in the middle 50s to near 60 degrees.\n\nWith the cold front will come chances of showers and some \nthunderstorms. The latest model blend has trended downward a \nlittle with the overall rain chances and rainfall amounts, which\nare now from a few hundredths to near a quarter of an inch. \nScattered showers and a few thunderstorms (30-60% chances) will \nspread into southern Illinois, southwest Indiana and much of \nsoutheast Missouri Sunday night. Monday morning may be fairly \nquiet, but chances crank back up to 30-50% across our entire \nregion Monday afternoon with the heat of the day. 20-30% chances\nwill taper off from west to east Monday night, with thunder \npotential ending by late evening. Beyond Monday night, dry \nconditions are expected through Saturday.",
